                        Java OOPs With Exception LLD Project — Parking Lot Management System

A driver arrives with a car or a bike. The parking lot assigns a free spot and issues a ticket. When the driver leaves, 
the system calculates the fee, closes the ticket, and frees the spot for the next vehicle.

1. Requirements
- Park a car or bike in an available spot.
- Reject a vehicle that is already parked or when the lot is full.
- Charge ₹40 per hour for a car and ₹20 per hour for a bike. Round partial hours up, with a minimum charge of one hour.
- Free the spot when the driver exits. Reject a ticket that has already been used.


2. Class design

Class	                         Responsibility
Vehicle	:-                    Stores the registration number and defines calculateParkingFee()
Car, Bike	:-                  Implement their own parking rates
ParkingSpot	:-                Stores the vehicle currently occupying a numbered spot
ParkingTicket :-             	Records the ticket ID, spot number, and entry time
ParkingLot :-               	Assigns spots, tracks active tickets, and handles exits

